{"ocrText": "women who were childlike, and Jane always enjoyed childhood\nso. She would have been perfectly happy to remain a child.\nWith Lucy,\nit was another matter. Her father influenced her\nmuch more. They weren't close, but he never begrudged giv-\ning her time. Jane seemed to bore him. He and Lucy did seem\nto have some relationship.\nIt upset her very much when he left.\nShe latched on to Hildon, and stayed attached to him.\nThey were once so naive that they thought the paisley sheets\nwould make them pregnant. There they were on the floor in\nthe morning, because they wouldn't\nlie on the sheets.\nIt was\none of those mysterious tableaux of childhood that didn't get\nexplained until years later.\nThey were so busy when they were children that Rita could\nstill not believe that they had grown up and done whatever\nthey could to avoid work. They liked doing things of all sorts.\nTheir days were so scheduled, they barely had time for school.\nThey\nlived\nfor summer. Night, and summer. At night they\nturned their bedroom into the Old Vic. Jane's bedroom. Lucy\nwas always in Jane's room. One time she had a cap gun. Rita\ncould remember taking\nit away and wrapping\nit in newspaper\nas\nif\nit were a fish. Then she threw\nit away. Real guns or toy\nguns too often led to tragedy. She had read, recently, that some\nman had picked up his son's water pistol, when the paper boy\nwas being adamant about the money he was owed. The paper\nboy came back with a revolver and aimed\nit through the win-\ndow and shot the man in the back of the head. She believed in\ngun control, no matter what the hunters said. The paper boy\nwith the gun had no more trouble\ngetting\nit than\na person\nwould have going out to buy\na candy\nbar. He was thirteen\nyears old.\nShe understood that she was not to think about what went\non in the world. That the New York Times no more reflected\nthe problems of the day than a statement made by the Queen\nof Hearts. She was not supposed to embarrass people by read-\ning the paper and telling them what she had read.\nDear Lucy\u2014/ try not to think ofJane as dead. Frankly, this\nmeans, lately, that\nI try not to think about Jane.\nJane probably\ngot too much\nattention.\nPeople would\nsay,\n218", "textLayer": [{"text": "women", "x": 13.03, "y": 4.49, "w": 8.86, "h": 2.24, "fontSize": 11.2}, {"text": "who", "x": 22.89, "y": 4.49, "w": 5.21, "h": 2.2, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "were", "x": 29.0, "y": 4.72, "w": 5.88, "h": 1.86, "fontSize": 9.3}, {"text": "childlike,", "x": 35.78, "y": 5.01, "w": 11.23, "h": 1.42, "fontSize": 7.1}, {"text": "and", "x": 48.06, "y": 4.73, "w": 4.27, "h": 1.8, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "Jane", "x": 53.03, "y": 4.87, "w": 5.45, "h": 1.72, "fontSize": 8.6}, {"text": "always", "x": 59.48, "y": 4.75, "w": 8.25, "h": 1.74, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "enjoyed", "x": 68.67, "y": 4.75, "w": 9.62, "h": 1.74, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "childhood", "x": 79.24, "y": 4.72, "w": 12.32, "h": 1.73, "fontSize": 8.6}, {"text": "so.", "x": 12.99, "y": 7.39, "w": 3.03, "h": 1.28, "fontSize": 6.4}, {"text": "She", "x": 17.39, "y": 6.95, "w": 4.45, "h": 1.88, "fontSize": 9.4}, {"text": "would", "x": 22.99, "y": 6.84, "w": 7.68, "h": 1.94, "fontSize": 9.7}, {"text": "have", "x": 31.85, "y": 6.96, "w": 5.5, "h": 1.74, "fontSize": 8.7}, {"text": "been", "x": 38.53, "y": 6.92, "w": 5.69, "h": 1.8, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "perfectly", "x": 45.4, "y": 7.11, "w": 10.95, "h": 1.54, "fontSize": 7.7}, {"text": "happy", "x": 57.63, "y": 6.84, "w": 7.54, "h": 1.91, "fontSize": 9.5}, {"text": "to", "x": 66.4, "y": 7.14, "w": 2.32, "h": 1.47, "fontSize": 7.3}, {"text": "remain", "x": 69.86, "y": 6.88, "w": 8.44, "h": 1.78, "fontSize": 8.9}, {"text": "a", "x": 79.53, "y": 7.2, "w": 1.09, "h": 1.38, "fontSize": 6.9}, {"text": "child.", "x": 81.71, "y": 7.15, "w": 6.73, "h": 1.42, "fontSize": 7.1}, {"text": "With", "x": 15.92, "y": 9.05, "w": 6.3, "h": 1.99, "fontSize": 10.0}, {"text": "Lucy,", "x": 23.32, "y":